Auburn Botanic Gardens were opened officially by the Governor of NSW Sir Roden Cuttler on September 11, 1977.

Auburn Botanic Gardens are divided into eight sections:

Japanese hill and lake; 
Formal area, containing the reflection pool and pergola; 
Woodland theater and billabong area; 
Australian rainforest; 
Australian woodlands; 
Picnic and BBQ area; 
Aviary and 
Fauna reserve.

